gh the band and category summary loops, both iterate bands (fixed at 7) against N month-purchases, which is linear, not quadratic \u2014 same for the money formatting and text width calculations. So the slowdown probably isn't a straightforward algorithmic complexity issue but something else in how the statement is being rendered.\n\nBoth `the_mean_purchase_this_month` and `spend_summary` divide by the count of purchases, which would throw a ZeroDivisionError for shoppers with none this month \u2014 that's a correctness bug caught upstream, but doesn't explain a pure latency spike since p50 stays flat while p99 blows up. With only four files in scope, the fix has to live in either monthly_statement.py or spend_summary.py, so I want to recount the full-purchase-history iteration more carefully to see if there's a hidden nested loop I'm missing.\n\nMaybe I should try searching the repository for other terms I haven't checked yet, like \"sleep\", \"requests\", or \"time\", to see if there's something outside what I've already read.\n\n",
